            "description": "Watch Tondela vs irense highlights and goals from Primeira Liga on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on May 12, 2026. The Primeira Liga action continued on 2026-05-12 as Tondela welcomed irense for a highly anticipated encounter. Both teams took to the pitch with clear tactical objectives, looking to assert dominance in a match that would eventually be defined by clinical finishing and late drama. Aiko Gives Tondela the Edge The match began with irense attempting to dictate play, but it was Tondela who showed superior clinical edge. In the 18th minute, the deadlock was broken when Pedro Henryque provided a pinpoint assist for Makan Aiko , who slotted the ball home with his right foot. The goal energized the home crowd, and Tondela nearly doubled their lead just before the interval. In the 44th minute, Rony Lopes unleashed a delicate lob that beat the goalkeeper but rattled off the crossbar, much to the relief of the visitors. irense did have their chances to equalize, most notably a header from Kiko Bondoso that required a steady save from Bernardo Fontes . However, despite enjoying the lion's share of possession, the visitors struggled to break down a resilient Tondela defense, heading into the break trailing by a single goal. Lopes Seals the Result Amidst Late Chaos The second half saw Tondela maintain their discipline while waiting for the perfect moment to strike again. That moment arrived in the 60th minute when Tiago Manso set up Rony Lopes , who found the back of the net with a powerful left-footed strike to make it 2-0. irense responded with a wave of tactical substitutions, bringing on Luis Semedo and Cedric Teguia , but the hosts remained compact and organized. As the clock ticked towards full-time, the atmosphere grew increasingly heated. The stoppage time period was marred by several incidents, leading to yellow cards for Cedric Teguia and Jordan Pefok . The tension reached its boiling point in the 94th minute when the referee showed a direct red card to Maracas for unsportsmanlike conduct. Despite irense finishing with 60% possession, Tondela walked away with a deserved 2-0 victory, showcasing a masterclass in efficiency.",
